verset{⟷}{PQ}.$\n\n![](images/2e/2e48106e4aedb44faef00060f6af9632bd0c8e62eb8d06f12606c2a476bacac3.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186294980 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115336 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6a916099-a237-5612-b7f1-3679b7ff069d" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating an Unknown Angle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "250975f6-1855-51d4-855b-4756eab86379" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{30}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293090} {:answer/id #uuid "74682fc2-217c-57f5-ab98-c931310e5466" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{18}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293411} {:answer/id #uuid "7d0ac39b-3059-5c95-9035-fede9601ced2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{15}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293433} {:answer/id #uuid "c8f82474-ac34-5dcf-9935-8a82efc05435" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{20}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293712} {:answer/id #uuid "e390ae5f-9602-5bc0-bd7b-333ec91cd6ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{25}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293825}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c8f82474-ac34-5dcf-9935-8a82efc05435" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{20}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293712} :answer-field/id #uuid "5dff0f5f-38be-5491-8c48-4be6dc5f48b4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294264}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "94753d7f-95e4-5b39-9c21-ede7ecea7547" :question/math-academy-id "q-27832" :question/problem "![](images/66/6665784a8ce048fd26fbd97038346e8e6fdf6800d645ea0488f1c18986f5864b.png)\n\nConsider the triangle $△ABC$ shown above. The line segment $\\overset{―}{CH}$ is the altitude corresponding to $\\overset{―}{AB}.$ If $m∠BAC={110}^{∘},$ calculate $m∠HCA.$" :question/worked-solution "Since the straight angle must have a measure of ${180}^{∘},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠HAC+m∠BAC & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠HAC+{110}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠HAC & ={70}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $△ACH$ is a right triangle. Since its interior angles must sum to ${180}^{∘},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠HCA+m∠HAC+m∠AHC & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠HCA+{70}^{∘}+{90}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠HCA+{160}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠HCA & ={20}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
